# Binary control template for `make deb`. The Makefile substitutes @...@ and
# strips these comment lines (dpkg-deb rejects them in a real control file).
Package: veracage
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/emptyname-org/veracage
# @SHLIBS@ is dpkg-shlibdeps' output for the three binaries: libc6, libgcc-s1
# and libxkbcommon0, with the version each was actually built against. It sees
# only DT_NEEDED, so everything opened with dlopen is listed by hand below.
# util-linux (blkid, setpriv) is Essential, so policy says not to depend on it.
Depends: @SHLIBS@,
 python3 (>= 3.11),
 cryptsetup-bin,
 bubblewrap,
 pkexec | policykit-1,
 systemd,
 dbus-daemon | dbus-bin | dbus,
 passwd,
 mount,
# dlopened by the agent and the compositor: rendering, and the Wayland client
# side the nested compositor needs to appear on the Host session.
 libegl1,
 libgl1,
 libwayland-client0,
 libwayland-egl1
# fontconfig (fc-match) resolves the UI font, gsettings and xdg-utils read the
# Host desktop's font and mime settings: all three fall back if absent.
# The fsck helpers are looked up per filesystem type and skipped if missing.
# The X11 stack is dlopened only when the Host session is X11.
Recommends: fontconfig,
 libglib2.0-bin,
 xdg-utils,
 e2fsprogs,
 dosfstools,
 exfatprogs,
 libx11-6,
 libx11-xcb1,
 libxcb1,
 libxkbcommon-x11-0,
 libxcursor1,
 libxi6,
 libxrender1
Description: opens encrypted volumes into an isolated workspace
 Veracage opens VeraCrypt and LUKS volumes and keeps their decrypted contents
 out of reach of the rest of the Host. A small root helper opens the volume
 with cryptsetup and idmap-mounts it so its contents are owned by a dedicated
 veracage system uid, inside a private mount namespace. Every other non-root
 uid is denied by ownership, and the mount never appears in /proc/mounts.
 .
 Apps run as that uid under bubblewrap (no network, no host filesystem,
 curated /etc, --clearenv), rendered by a nested Wayland compositor that owns
 the clipboard and hosts the menu bar. Data reaches the Host only through the
 Shared directory or an explicit clipboard copy.
